From efd396588375358a8ce1ba294fe2f09bba4b8522 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:58:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: asynchronous execution and explicit stack
 size policy

The batch data and the rotation data get execution options
(`mfront_gpb_ExecutionOptions`), which hold the queue and two new
options.

- `statistics`: if not null, the statistics of the batch are accumulated
  in the given structure (`mfront_gpb_BatchStatistics`), which is
  accessible by the device. The CUDA, HIP and Kokkos backends then return
  once the computations are submitted, as the SYCL backend when no field
  is copied. The calling code synchronizes the queue. Several batches and
  other computations can thus be submitted before a single
  synchronization. The other backends accumulate the statistics on the
  host. C functions initialize and decode the statistics.
- `preserve_stack_size`: if not null, the stack size of the threads of
  the device is never modified, and an error is reported if it is too
  small. The stack size is a property of the context of the device,
  shared by all the computations of the process.

The modifications of the stack size are protected by a single mutex per
library, instead of one mutex per kernel.

The second step of the comparison tests is computed asynchronously.
